            <ArticleTitle>Repair of left anterior descending coronary artery perforation by Magic Wallstent implantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>304-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary rupture is a rare complication of percutaneous coronary intervention. However, it may be associated with serious hemodynamic consequences often leading to tamponade, myocardial infarction, emergency surgical intervention, or death. We report a successful percutaneous repair of a brisk left anterior descending coronary artery perforation by the implantation of a Magic Wallstent.</AbstractText>
